Add the opt-in --contextual-quantifier-domains option. With the refreshed type system, a bound variable of a forall or exists expression whose type is omitted, and whose every use is as an argument to function parameters declared with one subset type, gets that subset type instead of its base type, so `exists b :: Q(F, b)` with `Q(F: iset<T>, b: T)` no longer fails the subset check of `T` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/200).
